                {
                    "title": "Tumun",
                    "duration": "02:00",
                    "lyrics": null,
                    "label": null,
                    "track_id": 1974206830,
                    "track_num": "50",
                    "artist": "KR Seward",
                    "url": "https://aversiontoreality.bandcamp.com/track/tumun",
                    "trackCoverUrl_0": "https://f4.bcbits.com/img/a1455773487_0",
                    "art_id": 1455773487,
                    "about": "Everyone says and says again the most important thing in humor is timing.\nI like hearing stories, even funny ones. This in spite of being a world class introvert, aka total grouch. But I’m no good at telling jokes or stories. And just go on too long on the small bits. And get lost along the way.\nSo to show up at all is a timely thing.\n\"Maybe ah shudda sed DiMaggio?\"\nMaybe.\nI don’t tell stories, though I do like hearing stories.\nPunchlines are okay. Set ups are fine (“a priest, a rabbi, a minister and a dog walk into an art space. It’s noise improv night. And there’s a bar.”). But getting from one place to another seems counter to the game after Cage, La Monte Young and others. What middle? What punchline? Keep yur cadence to yurself, leave the frame open wide, etc, etc.\nNo idea.\nJust recall some bluegrass jamsters’ meet bearing the sign “no Dixieland-ing” . As the recursive middle of Eno’s Third Uncle sounds more and more like the Outlaws stretching out “Green Grass and High Tides” (It wuzz duh ‘70s. Go figure.) No end’s in sight. Melodies and riffs and scalar fusillades be danged.\nAnd so much for Xeno’s Paradox, say those infinite subdivisions of the finite that leave the arrow forever short of the mark. Now let us praise infinite subdivisions of the infinite. We ride the arrow, are the arrow. Perhaps eventually to arrive.\nLike clickbait speculations on the siippery bits of quantum mechanical physics, one must do yet more than rush or drag the beat. One must rub the beat till it smears out of earshot.\nStill, “must” is a pretty big word. The necessity is maybe ours. Mine, likely. Yours?\nPerhaps.\nSee you there.\n---------------------------------\nkrseward.bandcamp.com",
                    "credits": "from PROCRASTINOISE - an Electronic Cottage compilation, released March 1, 2023\nMade with Virtual ANS.",
                    "license": "Attribution Non-commercial Share Alike"
                },
                {
                    "title": "I'm Late",
                    "duration": "01:59",
