                    "art_id": 3015427877,
                    "about": "\"Gandy Dancers were those who laid track during the early years of railroad construction in the US. The track reminded me how they would wobble or \"dance\" as they manouvered the massive iron pieces into place. For this improvisation I used the Korg iMS 20 app, Korg Radias for the metallic shard sounds and a recording from my phone of a broken fan on the bus.\"",
